WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.130
The David Pakman Show at David Pakman Dotcom.

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:05.250
So there's a new propaganda war being waged
right now that was triggered by Donald Trump's

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:10.450
suspension from Twitter and is growing because
of the distancing that many for profit businesses

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:15.580
have decided they want to make from the right
wing social media app Parler.

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:19.759
And I have news for everybody who's furious
about what's happening to parler.

00:00:19.759 --> 00:00:22.439
WOAK mobs are not destroying parler.

00:00:22.439 --> 00:00:24.159
Regulation is not destroying parler.

00:00:24.159 --> 00:00:26.189
The government is not destroying parler.

00:00:26.189 --> 00:00:29.479
Hackers are not destroying parler.

00:00:29.479 --> 00:00:34.820
Capitalism is solely to blame for what is
happening to parler.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:38.230
Capitalism is responsible for Parlor's demise.

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:44.030
Apple and Amazon have removed parler from
their services because as for profit companies,

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:48.810
they can do whatever the hell they want, partially
because Republicans have refused to regulate

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:49.810
them.

00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:53.640
They are making business decisions that they
determined are best for them, and they are

00:00:53.640 --> 00:01:01.000
making these decisions within a free market
in which you and I as consumers can also decide,

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.540
wow, I don't like what Apple did to parler.

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:09.979
So now I'm going to boycott Apple or I can
decide, you know what I like what Apple did

00:01:09.979 --> 00:01:11.020
to parler.

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:14.470
I'm going to go and buy 10 iPhones if I want
to do that.

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:20.560
Google decided to remove Parler from their
app store because they say parler isn't sufficiently

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:21.950
policing user posts.

00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:26.079
And so a whole bunch of posts that encourage
and incite violence and crime are remaining

00:01:26.079 --> 00:01:27.619
on the platform.

00:01:27.619 --> 00:01:32.770
And there are people who are furious and saying,
well, hold on a second, Google is kind of

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:33.889
a monopoly.

00:01:33.889 --> 00:01:40.420
So how can you say, well, if they're not on
Google, on the Google Play App Store, then

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:44.259
you can get parler because Google has a lot
of market power.

00:01:44.259 --> 00:01:49.740
Well, where were these exact same Republicans
when Elizabeth Warren was saying we've got

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:52.219
to deal with the monopoly power of these companies?

00:01:52.219 --> 00:01:55.890
They were against it, these same Republicans
who now are saying.

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:59.070
But but but they have monopoly power.

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:02.009
They were against dealing with monopoly power.

00:02:02.009 --> 00:02:07.200
When we on the left were sounding the alarm
about the lack of antitrust enforcement, which

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:12.250
was allowing monopoly power to grow unchecked
in the United States.

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:19.710
So there's a real irony in that unregulated
capitalism and the legalization of pseudo

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:25.850
monopolies are responsible for the downfall
of this far right social media platform because

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:32.710
the party that has been asking for more capitalism
and more corporate freedom got it.

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:35.830
And now they're furious that they have that
freedom.

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:42.200
And it has led to a free market of ideas and
decisions in which many companies decided

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:44.540
we don't want anything to do with parler.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:49.940
Nobody's preventing the people at Parler from
hosting their own servers and paying for them.

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:52.270
That's how capitalism works.

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:58.980
And much like Fox News is now being destroyed
by the monster they created, now that Fox

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:04.460
News is not quite radical enough for some
people, Fox News is losing some of their own

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:07.110
radical audience to Newsmax and on.

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:09.670
That's the same mechanism that's at play here.

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:14.960
The only question I have is whether the right
is pretending not to understand this or if

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:19.680
they genuinely don't understand that this
is a circumstance of their own making.

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:22.770
No one's First Amendment rights have been
silenced here.

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:29.480
Everyone can say whatever the hell they want,
but there are for profit companies saying

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:32.190
we don't want anything to do with what Parla
is offering.

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:38.850
Amazon isn't required to provide hosting services
to parler when Parlo allows members to violate

00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:43.880
the terms and conditions for Amazon, hosting
Amazon will lose money because they lose parler

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:45.330
as a client.

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:47.450
But that's Amazon's call to make.

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:49.350
And by the way, let's go even further.

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:54.250
And massacre's, by the way, being removed
from places of business by business owners.

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:56.240
That's not government regulation.

00:03:56.240 --> 00:04:02.290
That's a company deciding what's best for
us is not to have anti maskers here.

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:03.880
That's something they're allowed to do.

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:10.320
DC rioters being put on no fly lists because
airlines have decided they don't want their

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:16.260
business or corporations saying you were at
the DC riots, you're fired.

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:18.230
We don't want you working for us.

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:20.340
That's the free market.

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:26.090
And lots of the people crying about free speech,
first of all, don't understand what it means.

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:32.840
And secondly, think that free speech means
freedom from consequences to your speech.

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:39.870
The consequences to your speech in the free
market are part of free speech.

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:43.910
The speech and the consequences are all part
of speech.

00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:46.940
And remember that when we want to talk about
the First Amendment, we have to be talking

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:51.180
about the government, which is yet another
detail that seems to be missed here.

